---
import Bench from "./Bench.astro";

const said: Record<string, string> = {
  stop: "Stop the run",
  skip: "Skip it and carry on",
  fill: "Fill in 0-0",
  record: "Record the gap",
};
---

<section id="decision">
  <h2>The decision: what to do when a site is silent</h2>
  <blockquote class="cv-ask">
    <p class="cv-who">The film's narrator</p>
    <p>Every check mark hid a decision Riley never knew was theirs to make.</p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>Here is the first one: what Kick should do when Dunmore does not answer. <span data-decision-said data-said={JSON.stringify(said)}>Run Friday under each of the four and compare.</span></p>
  <Bench id="bench-decision" controls={["design"]} show={["says", "counts", "table"]} caption="Friday: Dunmore's page is down. Choose what the collector does about it." />
  <div class="cv-chose" data-gate data-chose>
    <p class="cv-once">Run Friday under all four before you read on. <span data-chose-tried></span></p>
    <button type="button" data-chose-open>I have tried them. Show the comparison</button>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
  <p>Kick chose “Skip it and carry on”, a defensible default: the run finishes and seven schools get a table. Its cost is that the gap stays invisible until a coach calls. Stopping publishes nothing at all. Filling in 0-0 publishes results nobody saw. Recording the gap finishes and names it.</p>
  <p>Touchline chose the fourth, and wrote it as a rule about what success means.</p>
  <p class="cv-rule">A named gap does not fail the run. A run succeeds when the coverage record was written and describes reality, gaps and all.</p>
  <p>A run that cannot write the record has failed, because nobody can know what it did. Publishing is a second decision, made by reading the record: Friday's run succeeds under this rule, and its table still should not go out.</p>
  <div class="cv-flow" role="img" aria-label="The collector writes down every gap. The season view, the published figures and the next run work from what it wrote.">
    <div>Collector</div><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><div class="is-record">Coverage record, and a gap list in each season file</div><i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <ul><li>Season view: a notice for each gap</li><li>Figures: counted, out of played</li><li>Next run: what to ask for again</li></ul>
  </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cv-further">Go further, on a separate page: <a href="../01-collection-field-work/?from=decision#platform">How Touchline builds it</a>, which keeps that record true across reruns and interrupted runs.</p>
  <p class="cv-next">Kick would have kept a record if Riley had asked for one. Go back and ask.</p>
</section>

<script>
  const KEY = "touchline-m1-coverage";
  const bench = document.getElementById("bench-decision");
  const out = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-decision-said]");
  const said = JSON.parse(out?.dataset.said ?? "{}") as Record<string, string>;
  const stored = () => { try { return (JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY) ?? "{}") as Record<string, string>).decision ?? ""; } catch { return ""; } };
  const apply = (choice: string) => {
    if (out) {
      out.textContent = said[choice]
        ? `In the setup you chose “${said[choice]}”, so the bench starts there. Run the other three too.`
        : "You did not choose in the setup, so the bench starts on Kick's choice. Run Friday under each of the four.";
    }
    if (bench && said[choice]) bench.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("bench:set", { detail: { design: choice } }));
  };
  let started = false;
  const start = () => { if (started) return; started = true; apply(stored()); };
  if (document.readyState === "complete") start();
  else { document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", start); addEventListener("load", start); }
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[data-save="decision"]').forEach((input) => input.addEventListener("change", () => { if (input.checked) apply(input.value); }));

  const echo = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-decision-echo]");
  const echoChoice = () => { if (echo && said[stored()]) echo.textContent = `In the setup you chose “${said[stored()]}”, cold.`; };
  echoChoice();
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[data-save="decision"]').forEach((input) => input.addEventListener("change", echoChoice));

  const gate = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-chose]");
  if (gate) {
    const read = (): Record<string, string> => { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY) ?? "{}"); } catch { return {}; } };
    const write = (k: string, v: string) => { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify({ ...read(), [k]: v })); } catch {} };
    const tried = new Set((read()["bench-tried"] ?? "").split(",").filter(Boolean));
    const note = gate.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-chose-tried]")!;
    const button = gate.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-chose-open]")!;
    const show = () => { note.textContent = tried.size ? `You have run ${tried.size} of 4.` : ""; };
    const open = (focus: boolean) => {
      gate.classList.add("is-open");
      gate.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".cv-reveal")!.classList.add("is-open");
      button.hidden = true;
      gate.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".cv-once")!.hidden = true;
      if (focus) { const r = gate.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".cv-reveal")!; r.tabIndex = -1; r.focus({ preventScroll: true }); }
      gate.dispatchEvent(new Event("rail:refresh", { bubbles: true }));
    };
    bench?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      const d = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>("[data-bn-design]")?.dataset.bnDesign;
      if (!d) return;
      tried.add(d);
      write("bench-tried", [...tried].join());
      show();
    });
    button.addEventListener("click", (event) => { write("open-chose", "1"); open(event.detail === 0); });
    if (read()["open-chose"]) open(false);
    show();
  }
</script>
